Modifications:

- retained one application authentication flow, generic login failures,
  server-side revocable sessions, activity debouncing, and boundary-safe
  application errors;
- separated password credentials from users and used bounded Argon2id PHC
  values without Mattermost's legacy-hash migration requirements;
- replaced raw session tokens with separately hashed, short-lived access and
  rotating refresh credentials;
- added refresh-family lineage, transactional row locking, reuse detection, and
  family-wide session revocation;
- retained Mattermost's dedicated per-model stores and reusable conformance
  tests while adapting them to Proctor's split credential schema;
- replaced product-specific API handler state with an immutable, minimal
  request principal and explicit per-route authentication classifications;
- accept credentials only through a single Authorization bearer header and
  never through URL query parameters.

